  "revised": "2026-11-10",
  "source": "Neuron M303 Modbus map v2.0, Unipi technology",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Neuron M303 Modbus map",
      "version": "2.0",
      "url": "https://kb.unipi.technology/_media/files:products:neuron:unipi-neuron-m303-modbus-map-v2.0.pdf",
      "note": "Registers and Coils sections and description tables; listed on https://kb.unipi.technology/en:hw:04-extensions:downloads"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Addresses are those of the column 'Via Unit 0' (Modbus TCP unit id 0), where the sections of a Neuron controller share one address space: section 1 starts at 0, section 2 at 100, section 3 at 200, and so on. The document also gives per-section addresses for unit ids 1, 2 and 3, which are not used here.",
    "Unipi Neuron uses Modbus TCP. By default the Modbus server listens only on the loopback interface; it can be opened to other interfaces by changing its systemd script (document, Brief protocol description). The TCP port and the unit id used here are not stated in the document: 502 is the Modbus default.",
    "Registers marked Reserved or Obsolete in the document, and those named (Internal), are left out. Multi-register values are big-endian (most significant register first). The document types Real as a two-register floating point value, read here as float32; its text about half and single precision is ambiguous.",
    "Coils (suffix (coil)) repeat digital inputs, outputs and some settings that also appear as bits of holding registers. Analog values are in the unit selected by the analog input or output configuration register; the document gives no unit for them. Storage - Vendor specific 1 to 3 depend on the microSD card (Swissbit pSLC: card series, unrecoverable CRC errors, wear level threshold %).",
    "Some registers (the RS485 line configuration) have no address in the Via Unit 0 column; they are included for section 1 with the Via Unit 1 address, which is identical, and left out for the other sections. Registers whose name carries no I/O index are repeated in every section; the name then ends with (section N)."
  ],
  "protocol": "tcp",
  "port": 502,
  "unit_id": 0,
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 0,
  "enums": {
    "ao_mode": {"0": "Voltage 0 – 10V", "1": "Current 0 – 20mA", "3": "Resistance 0 – 2kΩ"},
    "ai_mode_ui": {"0": "Voltage 0 – 10V", "1": "Current 0 – 20mA"}
  },
